t from  brute force to the supernatural is a  curious one and it'll be interesting to  see how it plays out on the big screen a  trailer also makes a deliberate attempt  to compare Mulan to a Phoenix which  traditionally sits at the right hand of  the Emperor and is his guardian and his  protector while also showing the witch  literally turning into a bird of prey  indicating a foul showdown of some sort  or another is afoot on top of that one  of the trailers even showcases a duel  between the two female warriors of  course what would a Mulan remake be  without the guardian of lost souls the  eddie murphy voiced moo shu is one of  the most fondly remembered elements of  the original animated classic you demand  moo shu superfans should be careful  before they get their hopes too high  when it comes to the remake though while  the fan blogged is insider did report  that a source had claimed the little guy  would be in the film very little  information has come out about what his  actual role would be will we see the  powerful the pleasurable the  indestructible moo shu or will we see a  live-action alternative that is more  subdued and subtle maybe we won't get an  actual character at all but merely a  quick glimpse of a small dragon statue  or some other easter egg so far no one  is reported to have been cast in the  role which doesn't bode well for a  direct adaptation from the 90s original  however fans can take comfort in the  fact that the cast list does contain an  entry for a character named cricket  which hints that perhaps Mushu sidekick  crickey will somehow be represented the  official trailer seems to heavily imply  that the story will be steering into the  Mulan the Phoenix angle pretty hard  it even cuts to a shot of a live Phoenix  while Milan's father is asking the  ancestors to protect her perhaps instead  of seeing no protector will simply be  seeing Mushu swapped out for a more  appropriately epic Phoenix Guardian  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more Luper videos about  your favorite style for coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bells so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

